Production failures in `src/` must throw `AppError` from `src/errors/appError.ts` (or a subclass of it). Do not throw bare `Error`. Each failure needs a stable `code` (`<domain>.<reason_snake>`), a technical `message` (why/what/how for logs), JSON-safe `context` for ids/paths/env names, and `cause` when wrapping. Domain classes (`WebhookParseError`, `StaleHeadPushError`, `WorkItemPayloadValidationError`) extend `AppError` and keep their names for `instanceof`. Never put `AppError.message` on PR-facing surfaces. Use separate plain-English constants. Prefer `errorLogFields` / `serializeAppError` when logging failures; these produce the canonical recursively sanitized representation, and logging/analytics boundaries sanitize forwarded Error values and metadata as a final guard.
